From 70f00fe37494a657fa0e7586b275fa4369d776d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: why-research <why-research@localhost>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:05:57 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 06/12] exp/sm120 p06: EXPERTS_IN_ONE_LAUNCH 1 -> 0: the
 one-launch MoE kernel k_grouped_blocks needs > 132 KB of dynamic shared
 memory (its static_assert names compute capability 9.0's 227 KB)

Semantics: Selects upstream's own other form: the host loop over experts, which calls cuBLAS int8 GEMMs (exact on sm_120 per the A2 probe). Upstream's comment: 'Both forms are meant to give the same sums.'
---
 prover/weights_blocks/experts.cuh | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/prover/weights_blocks/experts.cuh b/prover/weights_blocks/experts.cuh
index d44cb1df..f771a9cb 100644
--- a/prover/weights_blocks/experts.cuh
+++ b/prover/weights_blocks/experts.cuh
@@ -48,7 +48,7 @@
 // alone. Both forms are meant to give the same sums.
 // Three tests that are not part of this repository compare the sums with a plain kernel's: two
 // test the selected form, and one tests both forms (it builds only at 1).
-#define EXPERTS_IN_ONE_LAUNCH 1
+#define EXPERTS_IN_ONE_LAUNCH 0 // exp/sm120: was 1; pk::Tile4<NL,NS>::SMEM is tiled for sm_90's 227 KB (two 66,048 B weight buffers alone exceed sm_120's 101,376 B)
 #if EXPERTS_IN_ONE_LAUNCH
 #include "weights_blocks/experts_in_one_launch.cuh"
 #endif
